  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Between your opponent and the goal",
  "description": "Play 5 v 5 or 7 v 7 with goalkeepers on a smaller pitch. Normal rules with one addition: when a team loses the ball, everyone in it gets back as quickly as possible and stands between their nearest opponent and their own goal.\n\nNow and then, a few seconds after a turnover, the coach shouts \"Freeze!\". Everyone stops where they are and looks: is everyone in the team that lost the ball on the right side? If so, that team gets a point; if not, the opponents get one. Then play on from the same spot.\n\nVariant: a goal scored straight from a counter-attack after a turnover counts double. That makes getting back quickly worth it. Play offside if you do in matches. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn and run back as soon as the ball is lost. Don't wait to see what happens."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Run towards your own goal, not towards the ball. Get between your opponent and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The player nearest the ball puts pressure on it, so the others have time to get back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Look over your shoulder as you run, so you know where your opponent is."
    }
  ],
